{"id": "whplitvice", "name": "Plitvice Lakes National Park", "short": "Plitvice Lakes", "place": "Croatia", "lat": 44.9, "lon": 15.6, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Croatia", "blurb": "Beech-fir forest and mossy tufa dams that hold back a chain of lakes.", "tip": {"id": "wolf", "title": "Remove the wolves", "text": "Wolves and lynx both hunt roe deer. Set Grey wolf to -100% and watch roe deer, then the beech they browse and the ravens that feed on kills."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Plitvice Lakes National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plitvice_Lakes_National_Park"}, {"title": "UNESCO World Heritage: Plitvice Lakes National Park", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/98/"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Eurasian lynx", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurasian_lynx"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Grey wolf", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_wolf"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Brown bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_bear"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: White-throated dipper", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White-throated_dipper"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Plitvice Lakes National Park", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "icon": "water", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.06, "desc": "Light reaching the forest floor and the clear lake water drives growth of trees, mosses and algae."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "heavy rainfall", "xh": 0.24, "wiki": "Precipitation", "desc": "The area gets about 1,500 mm of precipitation a year, which feeds the rivers that form the lakes."}, {"id": "karst", "sp": "lime-rich karst water", "xh": 0.42}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil and nutrients", "xh": 0.62}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "fungi and decomposers", "xh": 0.84}, {"id": "beech", "sp": "fagus sylvatica", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "Dominant tree of the park forests, which Wikipedia says cover about three quarters of the area. Its seeds feed dormice, squirrels, voles, deer and bears.", "ic": "willow"}, {"id": "fir", "sp": "abies alba", "xh": 0.32, "desc": "Grows with beech in the old-growth stands of Corkova uvala, where some trees are about 700 years old. Its seeds are food for squirrels."}, {"id": "moss", "sp": "bryophyta", "xh": 0.6}, {"id": "algae", "sp": "cyanobacteria", "xh": 0.82}, {"id": "roedeer", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.06, "desc": "Browses beech, herbs and shrubs. It is the main prey of the lynx in Europe and a regular prey of wolves."}, {"id": "dormouse", "sp": "glis glis", "xh": 0.2, "wiki": "Edible dormouse"}, {"id": "bankvole", "sp": "myodes glareolus", "xh": 0.34, "desc": "A common small forest rodent of the park area that eats seeds, fruit and green plants and feeds many predators."}, {"id": "squirrel", "sp": "sciurus vulgaris", "xh": 0.48, "name": "Eurasian red squirrel", "desc": "Feeds on tree seeds such as beech nuts and fir seeds."}, {"id": "gammarus", "sp": "gammarus", "xh": 0.68}, {"id": "caddis", "sp": "trichoptera", "xh": 0.86}, {"id": "badger", "sp": "meles meles", "xh": 0.12}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A scavenger that feeds on carcasses of deer and other animals killed by predators or the winter."}, {"id": "trout", "sp": "salmo trutta", "xh": 0.52, "desc": "Wikipedia says two native brown trout forms live in the lakes. They feed on aquatic invertebrates."}, {"id": "dipper", "sp": "cinclus cinclus", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "otter", "sp": "lutra lutra", "xh": 0.88, "wiki": "European otter", "desc": "Hunts fish, frogs and other water animals in rivers and lakes."}, {"id": "wolf", "sp": "canis lupus", "xh": 0.2, "name": "Grey wolf", "wiki": "Grey wolf", "desc": "One of three large carnivores in the park. In Europe it hunts mainly roe deer, red deer and wild boar and 